# .git is intentionally NOT excluded here (unlike the usual convention) -
# CMakeLists.txt captures `git rev-parse --short HEAD` at configure time
# to stamp DISPLAYCLUSTER_GIT_VERSION into every process's startup log
# line, specifically so a running/crashed deployment can be tied back to
# an exact source state. Excluding .git from the build context makes that
# git command fail silently (falls back to "unknown"), which is worse
# than the modest image-size cost of keeping it - this Dockerfile builds
# and runs from the same single-stage image, so there's no later stage to
# strip .git from even if excluding it from just the build step were
# enough.
build/
configuration.json
set.env
test.dcx
*.dcx
